# Terms of Use

Last updated: 11 October 2026

By using StreamSetu you agree to these terms.

## What StreamSetu is

StreamSetu is a media player. It includes no channels, movies, series or playlists, and it does not provide, sell, host or recommend any content. You add playlists and accounts that you have the right to use, and StreamSetu plays them.

## Your responsibilities

- Only add playlists, accounts and streams that you are legally entitled to access.
- You are responsible for the content you play and for following the laws that apply to you and the terms of your provider.
- Do not use StreamSetu to infringe copyright or to get around any protection on content.

## Licence

You may use StreamSetu for personal, non-commercial use on devices you own or control. The software is licensed to you, not sold. Components from other authors are provided under their own licences, listed under Open-Source Licenses.

## Third-party services

Optional features use services run by others (for example The Movie Database, Apple iTunes and iCloud, and YouTube). Their terms apply to your use of them. Artwork and details from TMDB are provided by TMDB. This product uses the TMDB API but is not endorsed or certified by TMDB.

## No warranty

StreamSetu is provided as it is, without warranty of any kind. Streams depend on your provider and your network, and playback is not guaranteed.

## Limit of liability

To the extent the law allows, the makers of StreamSetu are not liable for any loss arising from its use, including loss of data or content you add or any action taken by your provider.

## Changes

These terms may change. The current version is always in the app and on the website. Continuing to use StreamSetu after a change means you accept it.

## Contact

